# React & Node Patterns

## React

- Use functional components and hooks; no class components
- Colocate component-specific logic in custom hooks when reused
- Prefer named exports for components; default export only for pages/routes if the framework requires it
- Keep components small; split when JSX or logic grows hard to follow

## Node / API (when present)

- Validate input at route boundaries
- Return consistent error shapes: `{ error: string }` with appropriate HTTP status
- Use environment variables for config; never hardcode secrets

## Examples

```tsx
// Prefer extracting reusable logic
function useLanguageDeck(languages: string[]) {
  const [active, setActive] = useState(languages[0]);
  return { active, setActive };
}
```

```ts
// API error handling
res.status(400).json({ error: "Language code is required" });
```
